  "id": "QP03Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Tonsillectomy",
  "description": "A tonsillectomy is surgical removal of your tonsils (lymph tissue at the back of your throat) to treat recurrent infections, severe obstructive sleep apnea, or other problems. Your ENT surgeon removes both tonsils under general anesthesia. The procedure reduces throat infections and may improve sleep quality and breathing. Recovery typically takes one to two weeks with pain, difficulty swallowing, and activity restrictions. This type of procedure can be performed on both adults and children, and the cost may vary depending on the patient's age group.",
